  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Chandramohan vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... on 24 September, 2024 Author: R.Vijayakumar Bench: R.Vijayakumar W.P.(MD).No.203 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 24.09.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice R.Vijayakumar W.P(MD)No.20353 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD)No.17259, 17260 & 17261 of 2024 1.M.Chandramohan, 2.S.Rajkumar, 3.K.V.Saravanan, 4.S.Chandra Seker, 5.V.Rajesh Kumar. ... Pet vs 1.The Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration, O/o. the Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration, Dms Campus, Annasalai, Chennai 600 006. 2.The Member Secretary, Tamil Nadu Medical Services Recruitment Board, Dms Building No.359, Annasalai, Teynampet, Chennai 600 006. 3.The Secretary to Government, Health and Family Welfare (M1) Department Secretariat, Chennai 9 . 1/8 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis M.Chandramohan vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... on 24 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/30249502/ 1 W.P.(Md).N 4.Tamil Nadu State Food Safety Officers Welfare Associations, (Reg. No.190/2012), Rep. by the General Secretary P.Senthil Kumar, No.27A, Venkata Lakshmi Nagar, Trichy Road, Singanallur, Coimbatore 641 005. ... Responden [R3 is suo motu impleaded vide order dated 02.09.2024 in W.P.(MD)No.20353 of 2024] [R4 is impleaded vide order dated 24.09.2024 in W.M.P.(Md) No.19341 of 2024] Prayer: Writ Petition is filed under Article 226 of the Constitutio India, to issue a writ of Certiorarified Mandamus to call for the r pertaining to the impugned order of revised provisional selection l 02/Mrb/2021 dated 21.08.2024 on the file of the respondent No.2 and the same as illegal and consequently to direct the respondents No.1 settle the service conditions of the petitioners / existing Food Sa who are working in the Department from 20.09.2011 with necessary absorption in the newly created department called Tamil Nadu State Safety and Drug Administration Department prior to issuance of appo orders to the newly recruited candidates based on the Impugned Revi Selection List dated 21.08.2024. For Petitioner : Mr.S.Louis For Respondents for R1 : Mr.Veera Kathiravan, Additional Advocate General asst. by Mr.S.Shaji Bino Special Government Pleader 2/8 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P. ( for R2 : Mr.V.Ramesh, Standing for R4 : Mr.B.Saravanan, Senior for Mr.K.Gopal ***** Order That apart, the direct recruitment notification has been issued only for the vacancies excluding the present Food Safety Officers. Therefore, the provisional selection list has been M.Chandramohan vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... on 24 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/30249502/ 3 published by the Medical Services Recruitment Board. The Writ Petitioner may not have any grievance over the provisional selection list issued by the Medical Services Recruitment Board for directly recruiting the Food Safety Officers.",
    "facts": "2. The Writ Petitioners herein were originally appointed as Health Inspectors under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act and they were governed by the concerned local bodies. Later, when the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 came into force, the petitioners were directed to act as Food Safety Officers under the new Act from 2011 onwards. The Medical Services Recruitment Board had issued a recruitment notification on 13.10.2021.",
    "arguments": "4. The apprehension of the Writ Petitioners is that though they are working as Food Safety Officers from the year 2011 onwards, unless their service conditions are settled by the Government, their seniority would be affected. Considering the provisional selection list and issuing appointment orders to the selected candidates would not affect the service conditions of the existing Food Safety Officers, since their absorption and seniority related matters are pending at the government https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 7."
  },
